sec.p:
Spearman’s correlation analysis was used to examine the relationship between dFNC time characteristics and clinical variables. The results are shown in Fig. 10. In the stroke group, the FT in State 1 was negatively correlated with Breg and FMA-LE scores, with the correlation with FMA-LE scores being statistically significant (r $= -0.5233$, p = 0.0453);

Fig. 10.

Correlation between FT and behavioral scale scores in dFNC state. (a) The correlation between FT of state 1 and BBS and FMA-LE scale scores. (b) The correlation between FT of state 3 and BBS and FMA-LE scale scores.
